cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Super Library in your research or writing pipeline, please cite it as below."
title: "Super Library: an agent-ready, source-traceable language library for AI research writing"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Super Library contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/asimfish/super_library"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-08-12"
abstract: >-
  A reviewed corpus of normalized terminology, definitions, sentence patterns,
  and usage boundaries for writing AI papers, rebuttals, related work, and
  technical translations, covering world models, reinforcement learning,
  embodied AI, robot learning, and vision-language-action models. Records are
  backed by primary-source links with an audited promotion ledger; original
  library records are dedicated under CC0 1.0 (see DATA_LICENSE) while code and
  documentation are MIT licensed.
keywords:
  - academic-writing
  - ai-research
  - reinforcement-learning
  - world-models
  - embodied-ai
  - vision-language-action
